From c1f31b7a559cc98edbe9f156d1b4d0d972122b71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: supply SHA256 tagged-hash primitives

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics. The candidate repair below
changes this boundary and requires new validation evidence.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Fast-path single-input CheckRegularTransaction duplicate-input checks,
coalesce BlockUndo disk writes, and optimize bulk mempool clear.

Original-Commit: a4ea86865414bbf4f98512bbd4460e2a42897acc
Original-Patch: ecash/020
Split-Concern: hash

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Compile tagged SHA256 primitives in lotus_v2_header at their own prerequisite boundary, link their existing common consumer target, and add independently computed Layer-1 domain vectors. The primitive implementation bytes are unchanged; the owning concern is moved before its overlay callers.

